Set of keys                                                             There is a set of keys here.                                            Brass lantern                                                           There is a shiny brass lamp nearby.                                     There is a lamp shining nearby.                                         Small bottle                                                            There is a bottle of water here.                                        The bottle of water is now empty.                                       Your bottle is empty and the ground is wet.                             There is an empty bottle here.                                          There is a bottle of oil here.                                          Water in the bottle                                                     Oil in the bottle                                                       Tasty food                                                              There is food here.                                                     Wicker cage                                                             There is a small wicker cage discarded nearby.                          Black rod                                                               A three foot black rod with a rusty star on an end lies nearby.         You don't carry the rod.                                                Little bird in cage                                                     A cheerful little bird is sitting here singing.                         Are you trying to catch the bird?                                       The bird is frightened right now and you cannot catch it no matter what you try.  Perhaps you might try later.                                  The bird was unafraid when you entered, but as you approach it becomes  disturbed and you cannot catch it.                                      You can catch the bird, but you cannot carry it.                        The little bird attacks the green snake, and in an astounding flurry    drives the snake away.                                                  The little bird is now dead.  Its body disappears.                      It's not hungry (it's merely pinin' for the fjords).  Besides, you have no bird seed.                                                           Oh, leave the poor unhappy bird alone.                                  The little bird attacks the green dragon, and in an astounding flurry   gets burnt to a cinder.  The ashes blow away.                           There is a little bird in the cage.                                     Velvet pillow                                                           A small velvet pillow lies on the floor.                                Batteries                                                               There are fresh batteries here.                                         Some worn-out batteries have been discarded nearby.                     Dwarf's axe                                                             There is a little axe here.                                             You don't carry an axe.                                                 The axe misses and lands near the bear where you can't get at it.       The axe bounces harmlessly off the dragon's thick scales.               Flaming sword.                                                          A sword with bluish flaming blade lies on the floor.                    Partly covered by the armour, you find a sword.                         You don't carry a sword.                                                As you draw the sword from it's sheat, the cell lights up               with a pale blue light, emanating from the swords blade.                Graphnel with rope.                                                     A graphnel is immoveably fastened in some cracks in the ground.         A graphnel with a suspicious rope coiled at the end lies in a corner.   "Spelunker Today"                                                       There are a few recent issues of "Spelunker Today" magazine here.       Giant clam  >grunt!<                                                    There is an enormous clam here with its shell tightly closed.           You can't fit this five-foot clam through that little passage!          A glistening pearl falls out of the clam and rolls away. Goodness, this must really be an oyster. (I never was very good at identifying bivalv- es.) Whatever it is, it has now snapped shut again.                     I advise you to put down the clam before opening it.  >STRAIN!<         You don't have anything strong enough to open the clam.                 The shell is very strong and is impervious to attack.                   Giant oyster  >groan!<                                                  There is an enormous oyster here with its shell tightly closed.         You can't fit this five-foot oyster through that little passage!        I advise you to put down the oyster before opening it.   >WRENCH!<      The oyster creaks open, revealing nothing but oyster inside. It promptlysnaps shut again.                                                       You don't have anything strong enough to open the oyster.               There is a ferocious cave bear eying you from the far end of the room!  You are being followed by a very large, tame bear.                      There is a contented-looking bear wandering about nearby.               There is a gentle cave bear sitting placidly in one corner.             The bear lumbers toward the troll, who lets out a startled shriek and   scurries away.  The bear soon gives up the pursuit and wanders back.    With what?  Your bare hands?  Against *HIS* bear hands??                The bear is confused, he only wants to be your friend.                  The bear eagerly wolfs down your food, after which he seems to calm downconsiderably and even becomes rather friendly.                          The bear is still chained to the wall.                                  The floor is littered with worthless shards of pottery.                 Key shaped metal piece.                                                 Heavy iron cauldron.                                                    A cauldron is standing on the floor.                                    A witch cauldron is standing in the fireplace. It contains some hot soupthat's bubbling ominously. It looks dangerous.                          A key-shaped metal piece lies on the floor.                             A curious key-shaped metal piece lies within the coffin. It must have   been guarded by those shadows that flew out.                            Black rod.                                                              Chained to the wall by a heavy iron chain is a pickaxe.                 There is a shovel chained to the wall in the same way.                  You can lift it and wield it, but not take it with you.                 What about the rest of it?                                              A three foot black rod with a rusty mark on an end lies nearby.         Large gold nugget                                                       There is a large sparkling nugget of gold here!                         Several diamonds                                                        There are diamonds here!                                                Precious jewelry                                                        There is precious jewelry here!                                         Rare coins                                                              There are many coins here!                                              Bars of silver                                                          There are bars of silver here!                                          Jeweled trident                                                         There is a jewel-encrusted trident here!                                Egg-sized emerald                                                       There is an emerald here the size of a plover's egg!                    Platinum pyramid                                                        There is a platinum pyramid here, 8 inches on a side!                   Glistening pearl                                                        Off to one side lies a glistening pearl!                                Persian rug                                                             There is a Persian rug spread out on the floor!                         The dragon is sprawled out on a Persian rug!!                           The rug flaps its free end softly. Could that be a magic rug, a flying  carpet? Try some words from 1001 Nights, that's where flying carpets    come from.(Or at least, try some connected with travel.)                Ming vase                                                               There is a delicate, precious, Ming vase here!                          The vase is now resting, delicately, on a velvet pillow.                The Ming vase drops with a delicate crash.                              There is nothing here with which to fill the vase.                      The sudden change in temperature has delicately shattered the vase.     You have taken the vase and hurled it delicately to the ground.         Rare spices                                                             There are rare spices here!                                             Golden chain                                                            There is a golden chain lying in a heap on the floor!                   The bear is locked to the wall with a golden chain!                     There is a chain locked to the wall!                                    The chain is still locked.                                              The chain is now unlocked.                                              The chain is now locked.                                                There is nothing here to which the chain can be locked.                 Golden eggs                                                             There is a large nest here, full of golden eggs!                        Five-armed chandelier.                                                  There is a chandelier standing here.                                    A five-armed chandelier made of gold, furnished with strips of          other precious metals, is standing on the table.                        It is impossible to touch it! Here must be powerful spells at work!     Scepter.                                                                A jewel-encrusted scepter sparkles in the middle of the room.           A scepter, wrought from mithril, inlaid with gold, and encrusted with   diamonds almost as clear as silmarils, lays on the table.               Pearl-encrusted chalice.                                                A pearl-encrusted chalice stands here.                                  In a niche there is a pearl-encrusted chalice, seemingly glowing. This  might be the Holy Grail, found at last!                                 Beautiful harp.                                                         A beautiful, gold-siceled harp lies to one side.                        There was an exquisitely carved harp, with gold siceling around the     frame, being played in the orchestra. It now lies discarded in a corner.Brass vessel.                                                           A brass vessel stands in a corner.                                      A brass vessel of some kind stands on the ledge. It is somewhat remini- scent of Alladin's lamp, but is inlaid with silver.                     Treasure chest                                                          The pirate's treasure chest is here!                                    Mithril coat.                                                           A mithril coat lies glimmering on the floor.                            A mithril coat lies on the tomb. I think it is big enough to fit you.   It is a garment of war worthy of High Kings!                            Sparkling ruby.                                                         A ruby sparkles in the middle of the room.                              A sparkling ruby is embedded in the ice. I think you might get it up,   if you want to.                                                         Silver circlet with large saphire.                                      A silver circlet with a large saphire glitters on the floor.            A silver circlet with a large saphire is placed on the table, where the silky, soft material shows it off to great advantage.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Diamond bracelet                                                        A diamond bracelet is discarded in a corner.                            A beautiful diamond bracelet has appearently been overlooked. It remainshalf hidden by some velvet strips.                                      *Tomb                                                                   A magnificent tomb is standing in the middle of the room. There are whatmust be dwarvish script around the edges. Chiseling around the tomb tella story about a great dwarvish king. The tomb is very heavy.            There's no spice to eat around here.                                    *Grate                                                                  The grate is locked.                                                    The grate is open.                                                      You can't go through a locked steel grate!                              Are you trying to get into the cave?                                    The grate is very solid and has a hardened steel lock.  You cannot enterwithout a key, and there are no keys nearby.  I would recommend looking elsewhere for the keys.                                                 *Steps                                                                  Rough stone steps lead down the pit.                                    Rough stone steps lead up the dome.                                     The dome is inclambable.                                                *Rusty door                                                             The way is barred by a massive, rusty, iron door.                       The way leads through a massive, rusty, iron door.                      The door is extremely rusty and refuses to open.                        The hinges are quite thoroughly rusted now and won't budge.             The oil has freed up the hinges so that the door will now move, althoughit requires some effort.                                                *Fissure                                                                A crystal bridge spans the fissure.                                     There is no way across the fissure.                                     *Stone tablet                                                           A massive stone tablet imbedded in the wall reads:                      "Congratulations on bringing light into the dark-room!"                 *Plant                                                                  There is a tiny little plant in the pit, murmuring "Water, water, ..."  The plant spurts into furious growth for a few seconds.                 There is a 12-foot-tall beanstalk stretching up out of the pit,         bellowing "Water!! Water!!"                                             The plant grows explosively, almost filling the bottom of the pit.      There is a gigantic beanstalk stretching all the way up to the hole.    You've over-watered the plant!  It's shriveling up!  It's, it's...      The plant indignantly shakes the oil off its leaves and asks, "Water?"  The plant drags its tremendous long roots from the ground, and dances a merry jig in the hole and on the walls. Thereafter it sighs, folds up   and withers into dust. I'm afraid it is quite dead.                     The plant has exceptionally deep roots and cannot be pulled free.       *Phony plant (seen in twopit room only when tall enough)                The top of a 12-foot-tall beanstalk is poking out of the west pit.      There is a huge beanstalk growing out of the west pit up to the hole.                                                                           *Shadowy figure                                                         The shadowy figure seems to be trying to attract your attention.        *Cave drawings                                                          *Chasm                                                                  A rickety wooden bridge extends across the chasm, vanishing into the    mist.  A sign posted on the bridge reads, "Stop! Pay troll!"            The wreckage of a bridge (and a dead bear) can be seen at the bottom    of the chasm.                                                           Just as you reach the other side, the bridge buckles beneath the weight of the bear, which was still following you around. You scrabble despe-  rately for support, but as the bridge collapses you stumble back and    fall into the chasm.                                                    There is no longer any way across the chasm.                            *Message in second maze                                                 There is a message scrawled in the dust in a flowery script, reading:   "This is not the maze where the pirate leaves his treasure chest."      *Volcano and/or geyser                                                  *Vending machine                                                        There is a massive vending machine here.  The instructions on it read:  "Drop coins here to receive fresh batteries." There is a gentle draft   coming from behind the machine.                                         *Carpet and/or moss                                                     *Throne                                                                 You just broke my back. You had better get out of here quick,           and wrap up the whole thing. I can help you only 5 steps more.          *Table                                                                  Who do you think I am? Atlas? If you can't give a more sensi-           ble order, I will be leaving!                                           The table is *MUCH* to heavy to carry.                                  *Cell door.                                                             The celldoor is locked.                                                 The celldoor is open.                                                   The celldoor slams shut behind you. There is no chance of reaching the  key hole on the other side. There is, however, a key hole on this side. *Parchment                                                              Near the entrance lies an old withered parchment.                       At your touch the parchment withers into dust. Something was written    on it.                                                                  *Rope                                                                   The end of a rope hangs down in the niche chamber.                      *Hook                                                                   A rope of somewhat suspicious nature goes from the graphnel down the    hole.                                                                   *Board                                                                  On a wooden board bolted to the wall is written in a fine               and flowery script:                                                                       ------------------                                                      ! J.R.R. Tolkien !                                                      !    was here!   !                                                      !  May 1st 1920  !                                                      ------------------                                    Behind the board there seems to be some message.                        Behind the remnants of a wooden board you see a message chiseled into   the wall.                                                               *Mirror                                                                 As you pass the mirror, you see a black and ominious figure there. Afterchecking behind you, you find you have seen yourself. That shaft must   have been a chimney!                                                    *Runes                                                                  *Barrel                                                                 There is a barrel with a tap standing here.                             There is a barrel with an open tap standing here.                       Splendid thing, that red stuff running out of the barrel.               The barrel is now empty of that delicious red fluid.                    A Persian rug is stuck in the ceiling beyond your reach by some         sticky gooey.                                                           Through the hole you see a profusion of leaves.                         *Stalactite                                                             In the middle of the floor, there is a small crack, just wide enough foryou to get through it.(But it was too narrow for the knight.)                                                                                                                                                           The healing was most immediate!                                         You don't carry the pill.                                               Too slippery. Besides, you've stayed too long. You're frozen to ice.    Are you mad? That tomb must have taken the efforts of 12 strong men to  carry.                                                                  I'm afraid it's rather solidly grown together with the walls.           A huge green fierce dragon bars the way!                                The body of a huge green dead dragon is lying off to one side.          The dragon looks rather nasty. You'd best not try to get by.            With what? Your bare hands?                                             Congratulations! You have just vanquished a dragon with your bare hands.(Unbelievable, isn't it?)                                               *Snake                                                                  A huge green fierce snake bars the way!                                 Are you trying to somehow deal with the snake?                          You can't kill the snake, or drive it away, or avoid it, or anything    like that.  There is a way to get by, but you don't have the necessary  resources right now.                                                    Attacking the snake both doesn't work and is very dangerous.            The snake has now devoured your bird.                                   On the floor a merry band of elves are dancing, forming intricate pat-  terns. They see you and beckon for you to come and join them. An orches-tra with gleaming instruments is at the balcony, playing a lively tune. As you walk towards the elves, they catch sight of the sword you carry  with you. With yells of terror, they fly from the flaming blade in your hand.                                                                   You go down to the dance hall floor. The elves turn suddenly out to be  orcs, all of them shouting and reveling at the way they fooled you. Theygrab their knives and hurl them at you. You stand a fair chance of land-ing a job as a pin cushion.                                             You stand at the balcony behind the orchestra. There is some unrest     among the musicians. Suddenly, it turns out that both the dancing elves and the musicians are orcs. Those in the orchestra are small and deli-  cate, they throw away their instruments and scurry out of the room. The others stand at the floor and throw knives at you. Their aiming turns   out to be exceedingly accurate.                                         Hovering slightly above the floor, a whitish apparition emerges before  you. A low, rasping moan is heard, the sound sends a chill all through  your bones. You can, somewhat undistinctly, hear words. It sounds like: "Give back, give back, oh give back my body to me. Nobody will pass whomwon't do so, nobody will pass on this way ..."                          The ghost sees the sword and, with a startled shriek, disappears with a flash. A strong smell of burning hangs in the air.                      As you try to pass the ghost, you are grasped by an unseen hand and hur-led back. The ghost moans: "You have been warned."                      *Troll                                                                  A burly troll stands by the bridge and insists you throw him a          treasure before you may cross.                                          The troll steps out from beneath the bridge and blocks your way.        Trolls are close relatives with the rocks and have skin as tough as thatof a rhinoceros.  The troll fends off your blows effortlessly.          The troll deftly catches the axe, examines it carefully, and tosses it  back, declaring, "Good workmanship, but it's not valuable enough."      The troll catches your treasure and scurries away out of sight.         The troll refuses to let you cross.                                     *Phony troll                                                            The troll is nowhere to be seen.                                        *Princess                                                               The princess is here!                                                   The princess is standing, seemingly waiting for you to observe          or perform something that etiquette demands. (Have you never met        royalty before?)                                                        The princess smiles to you.                                             On the throne sits a lovely elven princess, clad in some green garments.She eyes you warily.                                                    As you approach the throne, the princess jumps to her feet, frowns dis- approvingly, and departs through the draperies to your right,(or east), Did you never learn to wash your face when it gets dirty?               As you approach the throne, the princess stands up, waiting for you.    As you apparently cannot behave right in the presence of royalty, the   princess turns gracefully away and departs through the draperies to     your right,(or east).                                                   I'm afraid I didn't hear your command. Please repeat it.                The princess acknowledges your bow with a slight incline of her head,   and asks you in a warm and melodious voice if it was treasure hunting   that got you into this cave. I humbly suggest that you answer the truth,(that is yes), as it undoubtedly was hope of monetary gains that got youinto this thing. Any other answer must be at your own peril.            A two-ton rock-slab falls from the ceiling and hits you. You are left   two-dimensional and thoroughly dead. Watch your mouth!                  The princess nods her head, and tells you that is what she thought. How-ever, the elves are not accustomed to give away presents without being  sure the recipient has his wits about him. She will give you a riddle tosolve. If you make it, you can have the treasures you can find, as the  elves are adept at smithwork, and can make new ones. The riddle is from old Norse mythology: Three eyes, ten legs and one tail, and like that   they go to the thingvellir. Who are they?                               Your knowledge of mythology is not perfect. The princess shakes her headand tells you this is not good enough, and you have to try at a later   date. She leaves the room trough the draperies to your right, or east.  The princess smiles and gives a nod. She allows you to take the treas-  ures with you and wishes you well in your treasure hunt.                The graphnel cannot be moved out of those cracks.                       The rope is fastened to the graphnel.                                   The rope is fastened at the top.                                        Don't be ridiculous!                                                    I'm game. Would you care to explain how?                                (You wouldn't even manage to lift one of the toes.)                     The princess gives a shout. A band of heavily armed elves come running  to her aid.....                                                         Some red liquid in the bottle.                                          You use the water in the bottle and are now clean.                      There is a golden chain around the neck of the bear.                    You are leading a gentle cave bear by the chain.                        A red liquid is running out of the barrel.                              There is a bottle with some suspicious liquid here.                     You have now some oil in the vase.                                      The liquid poured so hard from the barrel that it shattered the vase!   The water tasted good. Some minerals and rather cold, but pleasant.     Are you sure you want to drink the oil?                                 That was American oil, you idiot!!YEECH                                 You can't be serious!                                                   The princess looks a little surprised as you turn your back. She sits   down on the throne again.                                               Black rod                                                               A three foot black rod with a rusty mark on an end lies nearby.         Interesting.  There seems to be something written on the underside of   the oyster.                                                             For crying out loud, the poor thing is already dead!                    You can't pour that.                                                    You have nothing in which to carry it.                                  You can't fill that.                                                    The dwarves' knives vanish as they strike the walls of the cave.        A bright fire is burning in the fireplace.                              You have nothing in which to carry it. Besides, it's very hot.          Well, if you have a crane or something, we'll try.                      They're rather heavy, you know. Get a moving company, will you?         They're solidly fastened. No chance of getting them of.                 I wouldn't recommend it. It will cost you broken fingers and other      unpleasentness. Desist.                                                 There is an old and bent hag standing by the cauldron, stirring the soupwith a laddle, and cackling and crowing to herself. As she catches sightof you, she lifts the laddle and advance threatheningly on you.         As you try to pick up the witch, she gives you a hefty blow with her    laddle, turns around and runs away. As she passes the fire, she tips thecauldron so that the soup runs out and extinguishes the fire.           As you throw the axe, the hag waves her free hand in the air. The axe   turns into a boquet of flowers, and this turns around and comes back at you. As it hits you, you discover that it's still an axe.               As you offer the magazine to the witch, she eagerly grabs it and hurriesaway, forgetting her cauldron and soup completely.                      The hag looks at your offering, and cackles something about you being anidiot, not to give her something more entertaining.                     As you are swimming along, there is a disturbance in the water. Suddenlya huge sea serpent surfaces just in front of you. This is dangerous!    The serpent lunges towards you in a mighty leap, and open its jaws wide.You suddenly feel a mighty torrent sweeping you into it's mouth. (( Can you hear me?? HELLO!! Helloo! hello .)) .......... Nothing? Hm.. Well,  that was another meal for that bigmouth. Lets hope he get hiccups.      I'm afraid it will be the other way around!!!!                                                                                                                                                                          He has disappeared!                                                     Are you a strong person, like Hercules? If not, forget it.              They're rather well secured to the throne.                              You might call them an integral part of the stone. What you suggest, arepretty nigh impossible.                                                 Take a cave? Do you know what you're talking about?                     It's rather fleecy, you know.                                           Golden chain and rope with graphnel tied together.                      A golden chain and a rope tied together lies on the floor. There is a   graphnel at the other end of the rope.                                  A golden chain, tied to a rope, is fastened on the maze side of the     waterfall. The rope is fastened by a graphnel on the opposite side of   the waterfall.                                                          Envelope.                                                               There's an envelope laying here.                                        An envelope stands on one of the dusty shelves.                         Small pill.                                                             A small pill is laying here.                                            Curious ring.                                                           A ring of some curious shape lies here.                                 There's a ring of a curious shape on the altar. It looks magical.       The gate is down.                                                       The gate is up.                                                         The coffin is closed.                                                   The coffin is open. Some dread feeling is creeping out of it's shadows. The vault door is closed.                                               The vault door is open.                                                 The gate is still down.                                                 As you opened the coffin, *SOMETHING* flew past you and away.           It's immovably fastened to the fireplace. She was a witch, you know.    Well, you'd better take the container it's in, I think! (It's rather    liquid, you know.)                                                      A pill is inside the envelope.                                          This ADVENTURE is based on the ADVENTURE originally written by Don Woodsand Willie Crowther, later expanded by Bob Supnik and Kent Blackett, andstill later expanded by Nils-Morten Nilssen and Svein Hansen. In the    present version some of the added features are taken from an article by Greg Hasset in Creative Computing, which added hitherto unknown parts   of the cave. Many thanks to Greg!! This version is reprogrammed by SveinHansen, and maintenance and extensions is presently handled by him.     The program is written specially for NORD computers in NORD-FORTRAN 77. As Svein Hansen is responsible for this version, any inconsistencies andnon-answers that might surface are best reported to him, either directlyor through RSH, Norsk Data A/S, P.O. Box 25 Bogerud, OSLO 6, Norway.    Personal message from Svein Hansen: Although I am responsible for this  version, some of the added features are not my own. They are the luna-  tic and weird outcroppings from the minds of the Studio 54 Hobbies Groupat the ND.10-54 community at NIT, Trondheim, Norway. Any nervous break- downs, downbitten fingernails and suicides etc. resulting from these    ideas  ARE NOT MY RESPONSIBILITY !! Blame it on that sneaking, no good  group that are ever trying to write more vile computer games.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            AAAAAA  II  EEEEEE  EEEEEE  EEEEEE  !!!  !!                             AA  AA  II  EE      EE      EE      !!!  !!                             AAAAAA  II  EEEE    EEEE    EEEE    !!!  !!                             AA  AA  II  EE      EE      EE                                          AA  AA  II  EEEEEE  EEEEEE  EEEEEE  !!!  !!                                                                                                   Hot stuff, man !! Are you trying to turn my CPU?                 Something is glittering far overhead.                                   Your cauldron is empty and the ground is wet.                           Your cauldron is empty.                                                 You don't carry any water.                                              You don't carry any oil.                                                You don't carry any wine.                                               Your cauldron is now empty.                                             Your vase is empty.                                                     You want to empty the cauldron? OK. Here's what's inside:               That's not what's in there.                                             The plant grows explosively, sprouting tentacles and arms and gruesome  things. It SEIZES you !!! It  *EATS*  you  !!!!!                                                                                                     ***********  Welcome to ADVENTURE!!!! ***********                                                                                               In this ADVENTURE you will meet DWARVES, ORCS, a TROLL,                 and various other inhabitants of THE GREAT CAVE. Remem-                 ber, there's only an overworked CPU and disc drive to                   help you, so don't get mad at some long response time                   now and then. Good luck, happy hunting!!                                                                                                                    *************************                                                                                                                                                                              There's a burly sentry dwarf in the room with you.                      There are two burly sentry dwarfs in the room with you.                 You are carrying a small leather satchel on your back.                  Well, you'd better come to an understanding with the dragon before you  can take that, I guess.                                                 As you swing the cauldron, a gentle breeze from the north suddenly      strengthens, (it might be an angry whitch blowing hot blasphemy!), gets inside your cauldron and carries it away to the southern shore. As you  managed to retain your grip on the handle, you are carried with it. As  the cauldron approaches the southern shore, the breeze lessens, and you are placed a little ungently on some rocks.                             The bottle of oil is now empty.                                         A small leather satchel lies on the floor.                              Small leather satchel.                                                  You don't carry a weapon.                                               It's pretty sifty, and well nigh impossible to hold.                    The Mountain King is seated on his throne.                              The Mountain King lies snoring beside his throne.                       Silly thing. You're not allowed to take that, you moron. The Mountain   King snorts derisively, gives a small gesture,                          The carpet has sunk to the floor and rolled up once more.               Your bottle of wine is now empty.                                       